================================================================================
Method registry provenance
================================================================================

Registry entries cite published methods. A citation records where a rule was
stated; it does not imply the cited author endorses this implementation, and it
does not transfer any right in the cited work. Rules are reproduced as short
factual statements of method, which is what a registry is.

Every entry carries a confidence field. Where an entry rests on an abstract, a
publisher preview or a secondary source rather than the full primary, the entry
says so.

================================================================================
Dependency license posture
================================================================================

To be recorded as dependencies are added. The intent is a light, permissively
licensed surface with a runnable core that degrades gracefully when optional
dependencies are absent.

================================================================================
Data
================================================================================

No subject data is included in this repository. The validation corpus referenced
in the documentation is held separately and is not redistributable in its raw
form: it is re-identifiable, and consent covers one subject.
